         "1. Process definition: evaporation of liquid water into gaseous water vapour through leaf stomata.\n2. Suction mechanism: generates negative water potential (transpirational pull) lifting water 50+ metres high in giant trees.\n3. Mineral transport: continuous upward water current delivers dissolved nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium from soil to leaves.\n4. Evaporative cooling: latent heat of vaporization cools leaf blades by 2-5°C during hot afternoons, preventing enzyme heat damage.\n5. Water regulation: removes excess water absorbed by root pressure.",
