         "A taproot system consists of a single thick, dominant primary root growing vertically downwards into soil with smaller lateral branch roots (e.g. gram, mustard, carrot); a fibrous root system consists of a cluster of slender, equal-sized hair-like roots arising together from the base of the stem without a primary root (e.g. wheat, grass, rice).",
